    "id": "417d8cac-3561-80ff-a34f-d175d9513460",
    "title": "Securing Endpoints: Configure Policies in ManageEngine Device Control Plus",
    "slug": "securing-endpoints-configure-policies-in-manageengine-device-control-plus",
    "summary": "Configuring a robust Device Control Plus (DCP) policy is critical for two primary reasons: Data Loss Prevention (DLP) and malware protection. Unrestricted USB ports are major vulnerabilities, allowing insiders to easily exfiltrate sensitive corporate data or accidentally introduce ransomware into the network. By enforcing strict access policies—like read-only permissions or trusted-device whitelisting—DCP mitigates these insider threats and stops automated attacks like BadUSB. Furthermore, maintaining strict peripheral control ensures organizations meet stringent regulatory compliance standards, such as GDPR and HIPAA, by providing comprehensive audit trails of all file transfers and device connections across the enterprise environment.",
